Not bundled, reached out of process
-----------------------------------

Archspace deliberately keeps copyleft and vendor code at arm's length: it is
reached over MCP as a separate process, never linked (ARCHITECTURE §8.3,
research §4, §6.5). Nothing in this section is distributed with the app, and
running such a server is the user's own act:

  IfcOpenShell — LGPL-3.0 — out-of-process MCP server, never linked
  ezdxf — MIT — out-of-process MCP server
  LibreDWG — GPL-3.0 — out-of-process only, if a user chooses to run it
  Autodesk MCP servers and the Autodesk Platform Services APIs — proprietary,
    operated by Autodesk; Archspace only speaks MCP/HTTP to them

web-ifc (MPL-2.0) is named in ARCHITECTURE §3.3 for the IFC preview panel. It
is **not** a dependency of this repository yet; when it lands it belongs in the
bundled section above.

